From 063f0a1a95e5a4a3af7f92459a4b4c4ef0494ee8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 03:32:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sync): export and import settings to a file system
 folder (#256)

Add a File System sync method next to GitHub Gist, as planned in #256:
the user picks the mode in the UI, the folder path lives in
syncLocalSettings.json, and the existing commands become Export / Import.

- syncLocalSettings.json gets "syncMethod" (GitHubGist | FileSystem) and
  "fileSystemSettings" { path, lastUpload, lastDownload }.
- FileSystemService (ISyncService) exports the same files the gist
  upload does (settings, keybindings / keybindingsMac, snippets, extension
  list, custom sync files, sync pragmas, ignore rules) as plain files that
  mirror the User folder, plus a cloudSettings timestamp file. Import
  applies them like the gist download: OS specific keybindings, pragma
  merge, extension install / removal, summary page, restart prompt, and
  restores this machine's sync.* options.
- Same safety checks as the gist flow: "already up to date" on import and
  export, a prompt before overwriting a newer export from another machine,
  forceUpload / forceDownload respected, files removed locally are removed
  from the folder on the next export.
- FolderStore writes each file atomically under a lock file (stale locks
  from crashed exports are taken over), refuses to overwrite an export that
  landed while it was running, never follows symlinks out of the folder,
  rejects names that could escape it and refuses folders that overlap the
  VS Code User folder.
- "Sync: Select File System Folder" command, Advanced Options entry,
  welcome page link, and a Sync Method select plus folder field with a
  Browse button in the settings page.
- Upload / Download commands are titled "Sync: Export Settings (Upload)"
  and "Sync: Import Settings (Download)"; command ids and Alt+Shift+U/D
  are unchanged. Auto upload, auto download on startup and the summary
  output work with the folder.
- Settings page data is URI-encoded so Windows paths (backslashes) no
  longer break the page script, and the page re-reads settings before
  saving a change so it cannot overwrite values changed by a command.
- README section and focused mocha tests.

Closes #256
